  "summary_en": "FDA de novo order classifying the Argo ReWalk powered exoskeleton, and substantially equivalent devices, as class II. It sets special controls: biocompatibility, electrical and mechanical safety, software validation, performance and clinical testing, user and companion training, and labeling. 510(k) premarket notification is still required.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Powered exoskeletons are classified into class II under the generic name 'Powered Exoskeleton'.",
   "Special controls cover biocompatibility, EMC/EMI, electrical, thermal and mechanical safety, and battery testing.",
   "Software verification, validation and hazard analysis are required.",
   "Clinical testing must address level of supervision and environment of use.",
   "Training program, detailed labeling and 510(k) premarket notification are mandatory."
  ],
